+id: dl-005-createpatch-emits-minimal-structural-diff
+type: decision-log
+title: "createPatch emits minimal structural diff"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+# createPatch emits minimal structural diff
+
+## Context
+Clients want to send only what changed between two document versions, not the whole document.
+
+## Decision
+`createPatch` walks both documents. Objects are compared member by member (`remove`, `add`, or a
+recursive diff); equal values (member order ignored, as in RFC 6902 `test`) emit nothing; values of
+different types are replaced. Arrays trim their common head and tail, diff the overlapping middle
+elements in place, then remove or add the remainder. Only `add`, `remove` and `replace` are emitted
+(no `move`/`copy`). Non-JSON input throws, following dl-003 and dl-004. Values in the patch are
+cloned.
+
+## Consequences
+Patches are valid and deterministic, and small for localized changes. Array diffs are not a minimal
+edit script (no LCS), so reordering a large array may produce more operations than strictly needed.
+
